00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:36.200
It's a big one-- has
some heavy hitters in it.

00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:37.530
Google created the project.

00:31:37.530 --> 00:31:38.990
They're one of the
biggest contributors.

00:31:38.990 --> 00:31:40.948
Microsoft's a huge
contributor, as is Omnition.

00:31:40.948 --> 00:31:42.950
A big, big, growing community.

00:31:42.950 --> 00:31:45.500
I'd be remiss to
forget about Postmates.

00:31:45.500 --> 00:31:47.548
They developed the
entire Erlang library.

00:31:47.548 --> 00:31:49.340
They make a ton of
other big contributions.

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:51.632
And there's a ton of other
smaller contributors.

00:31:51.632 --> 00:31:53.840
When I was making this slide,
I was a little worried.

00:31:53.840 --> 00:31:55.070
Like, I don't want
to leave out any

00:31:55.070 --> 00:31:56.570
of the smaller contributions
from other groups.

00:31:56.570 --> 00:31:58.810
These are just the sort
of the organizations that

00:31:58.810 --> 00:32:00.700
have committed the most code.

00:32:00.700 --> 00:32:02.940
We obviously a lot of
support for exporters

00:32:02.940 --> 00:32:05.910
and back ends that you can
send data to with OpenCensus.

00:32:05.910 --> 00:32:08.560
Most of those are maintained
by their respective bodies.

00:32:08.560 --> 00:32:11.500
Datadog contributed an
exporter for Datadog.

00:32:11.500 --> 00:32:13.733
I think Honeycomb built
their own, and so on.

00:32:13.733 --> 00:32:15.900
Some of them were built by
the OpenCensus community.

00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:18.150
But it's a big, big,
diverse ecosystem.

00:32:18.150 --> 00:32:19.920
What we're excited
about today is

00:32:19.920 --> 00:32:21.600
announcing that
another big company

00:32:21.600 --> 00:32:24.490
has promised to make large
contributions to the project.

00:32:24.490 --> 00:32:27.030
And so joining us
at this conference

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:29.685
and joining the OpenCensus
project is Dynatrace,

00:32:29.685 --> 00:32:32.310
one of the world's biggest, and
I think the world's biggest APM

00:32:32.310 --> 00:32:33.030
vendor.

00:32:33.030 --> 00:32:37.740
And to talk about that,
we have Alois Reitbauer.

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:38.724
Hand this back.

00:32:41.676 --> 00:32:44.280
ALOIS REITBAUER: Yeah, hello.

00:32:44.280 --> 00:32:47.610
I'm Alois Reitbauer
from Dynatrace.

00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:51.500
I'm leading op-- oh,
that's not the slide,

00:32:51.500 --> 00:32:54.970
but yeah, it looks good though.

00:32:54.970 --> 00:32:57.730
I'm leading open source
initiatives here at Dynatrace.

00:32:57.730 --> 00:33:01.550
And I think we had our first
conversation about a year ago.

00:33:01.550 --> 00:33:04.420
And interestingly, very
much from the beginning,

00:33:04.420 --> 00:33:07.390
I think we have
around the same--

00:33:07.390 --> 00:33:09.312
had the same ideas on
how this should evolve,

00:33:09.312 --> 00:33:11.770
and that we should really all
collaborate around collecting

00:33:11.770 --> 00:33:14.560
trace data, and that we
all have our own back

00:33:14.560 --> 00:33:17.842
ends that provide our own
benefits to our customers.

00:33:17.842 --> 00:33:20.050
And also for us at Dynatrace,
well, a couple of years

00:33:20.050 --> 00:33:24.760
back, we started to focus more
on AI and analytics, obviously,

00:33:24.760 --> 00:33:25.840
having the input data.

00:33:25.840 --> 00:33:27.382
And we want to give
all our customers

00:33:27.382 --> 00:33:30.910
all of the flexibility to
augment their data with what

00:33:30.910 --> 00:33:32.320
you can get via OpenCensus.

00:33:32.320 --> 00:33:35.204
And I think in the next slide--

00:33:35.204 --> 00:33:36.420
ah, yeah.

00:33:36.420 --> 00:33:37.020
Thank you.

00:33:37.020 --> 00:33:40.050
So, this is actually a preview
that I have taken directly

00:33:40.050 --> 00:33:42.200
out of our development
process here.

00:33:42.200 --> 00:33:45.660
What you can see
here is actually

00:33:45.660 --> 00:33:47.560
OpenCensus data in Dynatrace.

00:33:47.560 --> 00:33:51.250
So we are now on weekly calls
with the OpenCensus team,

00:33:51.250 --> 00:33:55.740
with respectively Google
and Microsoft here,

00:33:55.740 --> 00:33:58.440
where our focus is really
that we provide OpenCensus

00:33:58.440 --> 00:34:02.700
data as first-class
citizens within Dynatrace,

00:34:02.700 --> 00:34:04.890
and also providing
our input, especially

00:34:04.890 --> 00:34:06.330
around type span
builders who have

00:34:06.330 --> 00:34:09.059
high-level APIs for OpenCensus.

00:34:09.059 --> 00:34:12.709
